  "summary_en": "Malaysia's Civil Aviation Regulations 2016, made under the Civil Aviation Act 1969, comprehensively regulate aircraft registration, airworthiness, crew licensing, operations, safety management, incident reporting and investigation. Part XVI sets rules for unmanned aircraft systems, including small unmanned aircraft and systems over 20 kg.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Aircraft must be registered and airworthiness-certified; Director General is the competent authority.",
   "Part XVI (regs 140-144) regulates unmanned aircraft systems, small unmanned surveillance aircraft and UAS over 20 kg.",
   "Small unmanned aircraft (≤20 kg) are exempt from the registration requirement in reg 4(3).",
   "Mandatory occurrence reporting, safety management systems and accident investigation requirements.",
   "Offences and penalties in the Third Schedule; in force 15 April 2016, revoking the 1996 Regulations."
